fact WorkItem(id: "WI-619", description: some(value: "WI-582 introducer scan mis-targets 2-ary rule heads: collect_rule_tvar_names (load.rs) treats ANY 2-positional-arg head Fn as an equational head and reads type-args off pos_args[0] (the first ARGUMENT), so a '[t]' introducer on a 2-ary head (rule same_ty[t](?x, ?y) :- Eq[t], ...) is never collected — the guard doesn't fold, the tvar isn't bounded, and the rule silently loses its WI-582 desugar (found empirically during WI-618 /code-review: 1-ary and 3-ary heads work, exactly 2-ary fails). Fix: recognize the equational-head LHS by the head functor (eq/unify/struct_eq shape), not by arity==2. ACCEPTANCE: introducers collected on 2-ary heads; existing equational-head rules unaffected; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-03T16:13:25Z"))

